mods.Microlith57MiscellaneousMechanics.name=Microlith57's Misc. Mechanics
entities.Microlith57Misc/AreaSwitch.attributes.description.acceptEntities=The kinds of entity that this switch reacts to.
entities.Microlith57Misc/AreaSwitch.attributes.description.acceptStates=The "states of matter" that this switch reacts to.\n\nAny: Anything.\nPhysical: Only original physical entities, not recordings.\nRecording: Only recordings, not physical entities.
entities.Microlith57Misc/AreaSwitch.attributes.description.animationLength=The length of the icon spin animation, in frames. Must be at least 1.
entities.Microlith57Misc/AreaSwitch.attributes.description.awareness=The additional distance (added to "radius") in which the switch can 'sense'\nentities that might activate it. This has no gameplay effect, but it's a useful\nway to help players intuit what kinds of entity the switch wants.
entities.Microlith57Misc/AreaSwitch.attributes.description.container=The texture of the container that holds the icon, relative to\nGraphics/Atlases/Gameplay.\n\nBy convention, use a circle when the switch accepts anything; a diamond when it\naccepts the player; and a square when it accepts a box. Similarly, use a dashed\nline to indicate that the switch only accepts recordings. (Of course you are\nfree to disregard this, it's just an aesthetic guideline.)
entities.Microlith57Misc/AreaSwitch.attributes.description.destroyBoxes=If set, this must accept only Physical Boxes. When the area switch group is\ncompleted, it will destroy the box that's activating it.
entities.Microlith57Misc/AreaSwitch.attributes.description.icon=The texture of the spinning icon, relative to Graphics/Atlases/Gameplay. All\nframes (by default 6, but this can be configured with "animation length") are\nused when spinning; but only frame 0 is used when finished.
entities.Microlith57Misc/AreaSwitch.attributes.description.label=The session flag this area switch sets. Give the same to multiple touch\nswitches and switch gates to group them.\n\nWorks the same as the "flag" of flag touch switches from Maddie's Helping Hand\n(because that's actually what it is under the hood).
entities.Microlith57Misc/AreaSwitch.attributes.description.persistent=If enabled, the touch switch set a flag once all the switches in its group\nbecome active, meaning it will stay active if you leave and reenter the room.
entities.Microlith57Misc/AreaSwitch.attributes.description.radius=The radius of the area in which the switch can be activated. This is where the\ntick lines are drawn.
entities.Microlith57Misc/AreaSwitch.attributes.description.spacing=The spacing between ticks when they are positioned around the circle, in\npixels.
